{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgjP9apGxyhSsfRcEVmST","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_018fKtNiWK2BznCGGrq9FbB6","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"C:\\Projects\\ai-template.wt\\wi-983\\docs\\reviews\\wi-983\\003-ADJUDICATE-e19a5cd.md","content":"Adjudicated: e19a5cd1b\n\n## amendment\n\nJudged on the cells as shown: LLR-360 `Detail`, `Rationale` and `Title` (JUDGED-TEXT sha256:f7d840bc9fd63076), and TC-399 `Expected` and `Method` (JUDGED-TEXT sha256:591b3f625ff55d80), against the 0949bc275 anchor. The rung is released. To decide whether to bless, I read the new text upward to SR-186, which both rows now serve: its requirement asks that the stopping decision be recorded in the scoped decomposition record, and its rationale rules out a new machine gate. I also read it downward to the composer (`plan_briefs` `_STOPPING_INSTRUCTION` and the round block) and confirmed that each of the eleven arms-map tests is defined once in its module.\n\n- [MEANING+BLESS] LLR-360 Detail (Title and Rationale follow it) -> before: a decomposition round's brief carries the applicable perspective questions with one outcome line each, through the declared slot, once in a combined sitting; a non-round carries none -> after: the same, and a round's brief ALSO carries a named stopping-boundary line asking, for each retained chain, why further splitting would only paraphrase or duplicate. A round with no roster or no applicable perspective carries the line beside its no-perspective line. The line is no row-ruling or machine line, and nothing checks for it; a missing reason is a finding for the review of the verdict. A non-round carries no such line. The line rides the same declared slot. A combined sitting carries it once, after its last section, and says under which section the verdict writes it -> not the same. A correct build of the old text, a round brief with questions and no stopping line, fails the new text, which adds an output, a case where it appears even with no perspective, a placement duty for combined sittings, and a negative scope (no check). Title and Rationale only follow the Detail; the Detail carries the meaning. I would bless it. SR-186 calls for the stopping decision to be recorded where the decomposition is judged, and the line puts it in the verdict that judges it. \"Nothing checks for it\" matches SR-186's \"no new machine gate\" and the build, where the instruction text is advice and the verdict parser ignores the line. The slot qualifier applies to the line exactly as the already-approved sentence applies it to the questions, so \"every round brief carries it\" and \"only where the template declares the slot\" read together as before. Every clause binds to an existing test through the coordinator's arms map. It stays one decision, the composition of a round's perspective block. The line shares that block's slot, round test, combined-sitting placement and parse-neutrality, so a separate LLR would repeat all four. The row names no implementation carrier and carries no `shall`. Every previously approved sentence survives, either verbatim or extended only by \"and the stopping-boundary line\" or \"and no stopping-boundary line\". Gaining SR-186 as a second parent fits §4 \"Keep or mint\": the row's decision is unchanged, and the parent link is a traced cell.\n- [MEANING+BLESS] TC-399 Expected, Method -> before: verify the hat block's states (round/non-round, parents, tag widening, the authoring-tags routes, the roster cases, the slot, the combined union) and that outcome lines change no parsed ruling -> after: the same, and verify that every round carries one stopping-boundary line asked of each retained chain, whichever shipped template composes it and with or without a roster or applicable perspective; a non-round carries none; a combined sitting carries it once after its last section and says where the verdict writes it; and stopping lines change no parsed ruling. Expected now names both parents and requires that a round's brief asks for each retained chain's stopping reason -> not the same, because the TC now obliges new checks and a new expected outcome. I would bless it. Each new clause maps to a defined test: the shipped-template sweep, the no-hat round, the non-round negatives, both combined-sitting placements, and the parse-neutrality pins. \"Whichever shipped sitting template\" agrees with the LLR's slot qualifier, because the two shipped round templates declare the slot and an override without it is already pinned to compose unchanged. It names no carrier, and its approved clauses stand verbatim.\n\nThe rung is released and no row is held, so no CLARITY row waits on either one. The later act re-attests both LLR-360 and TC-399.\n\nVERDICT: MEANING rows=2\n\nSITTING: JUDGED kinds=amendment\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2126,"cache_read_input_tokens":235127,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2126},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5c376c8c-200c-488f-950a-1fb2b7b7f425","uuid":"9e290c67-c9cc-4e1a-b120-6708b77a3809","timestamp":"2026-11-05T07:25:35.729Z","request_id":"req_011CgjP9acrqDUBX7eM35Th5","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_018fKtNiWK2BznCGGrq9FbB6":{"file_path":"C:\\Projects\\ai-template.wt\\wi-983\\docs\\reviews\\wi-983\\003-ADJUDICATE-e19a5cd.md","content":"Adjudicated: e19a5cd1b\n\n## amendment\n\nJudged on the cells as shown: LLR-360 `Detail`, `Rationale` and `Title` (JUDGED-TEXT sha256:f7d840bc9fd63076), and TC-399 `Expected` and `Method` (JUDGED-TEXT sha256:591b3f625ff55d80), against the 0949bc275 anchor. The rung is released. To decide whether to bless, I re